<title>USA: McGraw-Hill buys 2 healthcare publications.</title>
<headline>McGraw-Hill buys 2 healthcare publications.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>McGraw-Hill Cos Inc said on Wednesday it had acquired Healthcare Informatics and InfoCare magazines and their related assets from Wiesner Publishing of Englewood, Colorado for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>Healthcare Informatics is the nation's leading healthcare information technology publication, while InfoCare magazine addresses managed care information technology needs, the company said.</p>
<p>The editorial and business offices for the magazines will relocate to Minneapolis where  McGraw-Hill's Healthcare Information Group is located, the company said.</p>
